	// - peaks: for j in 2..n-1, y[j-1] < y[j] > y[j+1]
	// - valleys: for j in 2..n-1, y[j-1] > y[j] < y[j+1]

	// We can use DP over positions.
	// State: position i (1-indexed), current y value, previous y value, count of peaks so far, count of valleys so far.
	// But we can't count peaks/valleys until we have 3 consecutive points.

