	// - We can check if position i is a peak or valley: y[i-1] vs y[i] vs y[i+1]
	// - So when transitioning from (i, prev, curr) to (i+1, curr, next), we can determine if curr is a peak or valley.

	// Let's define:
	// dp[i][prev][curr][p][v] = number of ways to have i vertices, with y[i-1]=prev, y[i]=curr, p peaks, v valleys among positions 2..i-1.

